-- title:
--   Ends and smooth-point stalks of a supersingular chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ (the last three hypotheses form the rigidity guard of the $q=2$ case). Further fixed data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$ (this is [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16)), a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa(A),M')$ over the residue field $\kappa(A)$ of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the rational places that are affine geometric places and whose $j$-value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa(A)$, an inclusion hypothesis $hle$ asserting $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ (the first is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, the second that of the function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$, the kernel of the indicated reduction of unit groups), and a chosen element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   The base layer consists of: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$; the hypotheses that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field; the hypothesis $h\kappa$ that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; that $\kappa(A)$ is algebraically closed; an algebra structure of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ on $\kappa(A)$ and the hypothesis that the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa(A)$ (the quotient of $\kappa(A)[x_0,x_1]$ by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1$) is a domain; an index $\zeta_{\mathrm{ix}} \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, that is, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and finally an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$, the hypotheses that $A_b$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring, and an element $\varpi_b \neq 0$ of $A_b$ generating its maximal ideal. The field $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$.
--
--   The assertion is then universally quantified over an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'/k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ subject to the descent hypotheses: the join of $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}$ of the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $F_0$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; and a linear-disjointness hypothesis, namely that for every finite-dimensional intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with all $a_i$ in the join $L(K') := \mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of }K') \sqcup F_0$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ then every $a_i = 0$.
--
--   It is further quantified over a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ together with an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$, subject to the chart axioms (all stated, none omitted): the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; $B$ is contained in $L := L(K_b)$; every element of $L$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient $B/\varpi_b B$ satisfies $\mathrm{Ring.KrullDimLE}\,1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime, in the sense that $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; the element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ obtained from the Laurent expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ via $\mathrm{coeffEmb}$ and the inclusion $hle$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and a special-fibre hypothesis requiring, for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on $\kappa(A)$, every witness that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa(A)$ is a domain and every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,\kappa(A)\,C_s$ (the fixed field of the subgroup of $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$-images of the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta' \in C_s$, inside the Drinfeld function field) such that $\#C_s = \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, $\ker\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, $\rho$ carries the image of $a \in A_b$ to the image of the residue of $a$ in $\kappa(A)$, every element of the quotient field is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$, the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements of the quotient field that lie in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa(A)$ in the Drinfeld function field, and $\rho$ is equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $f \in B$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f \in B$, the value $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f)$ equals $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   Finally it is quantified over a field $FSS$ with a $\kappa(A)$-algebra structure and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with reduction field $FSS$ — that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $A$, together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $FSS$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa(A) \to FSS$, and such that every nonzero $f$ has a scalar multiple $c\cdot f$ in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue — subject to the hypothesis that an element of $F_0$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it lies in $W_0$.
--
--   Under all of this there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa(A)$, an assignment $Q \mapsto S_b(Q)$ of subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, an assignment $Q \mapsto \varphi_b(Q)$ of ring homomorphisms $A_b[X] \to S_b(Q)$, an assignment $Q \mapsto \chi_b(Q)$ of ring homomorphisms $S_b(Q) \to \kappa(A)$, and an assignment $Q \mapsto D_b(Q)$ of sets of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the following properties.
--
--   First, $\#N = q+1$. Second, a place $Q$ fails to lie in $N$ if and only if $R.\mathrm{residue}$ of every element of $B$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$. Third, for every $Q \notin N$ the following thirteen clauses hold: the image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ sends the constant $C\,a$ to that image; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa(A)$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X)) = 0$; $S_b(Q)$ is local with $\ker\chi_b(Q)$ its maximal ideal; $S_b(Q) \subseteq L$; every element of $L$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_b(Q)$, $h \neq 0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and an element $f$ of $S_b(Q)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$ divides $f$ in $S_b(Q)$; for every $f \in S_b(Q)$, the residue $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_b(Q)(f)$ under $\kappa(A) \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; $R.\mathrm{residue}(\varphi_b(Q)(X))$ has $Q$-order equal to $1$; $B \subseteq S_b(Q)$, and $S_b(Q)$ consists exactly of the $f$ expressible as $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ such that the residue at $Q$ of $R.\mathrm{residue}(h)$ is nonzero; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of those places $P$ that are rational, satisfy that every $f \in S_b(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfy, for every $f \in S_b(Q)$, that the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ if and only if $\chi_b(Q)(f) = 0$.
--
--   Fourth, the discs are pairwise disjoint: if $Q,Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_b(Q)$ and $D_b(Q')$, then $Q = Q'$. Fifth, for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_b(Q)$ the order $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ is $\ge 0$. Sixth, equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every hypothesis $h\tau$ that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$ of $FSS$: the place $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\,h\tau \cdot Q$ lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and if $Q \notin N$ then $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_b(Q)) = \{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_b(Q)\}$ equals $D_b(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\,h\tau \cdot Q)$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the description of a supersingular component of the semistable model of the modular curve read off an affine chart: the regular prolongation determined by $W_0$ has exactly $q+1$ ends, and away from the ends each place of the reduction field carries a smooth-point stalk obtained by localising the chart, equipped with an étale coordinate, a residue character and a residue disc, all compatibly with the level automorphisms. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_two_of_dvd) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
